# dispatch-path.baseline — what one dispatch of each agent reads before it reads
# one line of the project's own work.
#
# HAND-EDITED, NEVER GENERATED. UPDATE_RULES_GOLDEN=1 rewrites
# `rules-emission.golden` and does not touch this file. There is no flag that
# rewrites it, deliberately: the golden records what the text weighs, this file
# records what it is ALLOWED to weigh from, and a baseline that followed the
# measurement would measure nothing.
#
# Three components per path, and the bound is their SUM against the sum of the
# three figures below:
#
#   agents/<name>.md          the agent prompt
#   rules emitted to <name>   every path `bin/fusion-rules <name>` emits, run
#                             from this repository's root — plugin rules, any
#                             project-side rules in reach, and the stilwerk
#                             voice profiles. Not the neutral-cwd measurement
#                             the golden takes: that one excludes project-side
#                             text by construction, and two of this quantity's
#                             three components are the project's.
#   CLAUDE.md                 the project instructions, charged to every path
#
# HEAD-ROOM IS ZERO. This is not a budget. A path's total may not rise above its
# row at all, and an addition of N bytes to any component requires a removal of
# at least N from the same path's total.
#
# ## The arming, 2026-09-09, and what it does NOT absolve
#
# Armed at `bb341360`, BEFORE the cut this instrument was built to hold, and not
# at it. A baseline armed at the moment of a cut absolves the cut.
#
# It is the second event of the three in `helpers/growth-bound.ts`
# `## Re-baselining: the three events at which a baseline moves` — an arming —
# and it is the fifth surface to obey that rule. What the arming absolves is
# written here rather than disappearing with the number: over the thirteen days
# from 2026-08-27 to 2026-09-09 the coder path rose from 154 440 to 188 256
# bytes, 21.9 percent, while the always-on core bound in
# `rules-emission-golden.test.ts` stayed green throughout — 43 percent of the
# rise was `CLAUDE.md`, which that bound does not measure, and the rest was in
# rule files outside the universal core it does. Every one of the fifteen rows
# the fleet had at the 2026-09-09 arming therefore carried growth nobody cut.
# That is the state this bound is armed on, and it is stated so that a later
# reader can see the request the instrument stopped being able to make.
#
# THE GAP IN THE RULE, NAMED RATHER THAN CLOSED. The three-event rule was
# written for a surface fusion owns, and two thirds of this quantity is the
# project's. It has NO EVENT for a project that legitimately needs a larger
# `CLAUDE.md`. No fourth event is added: inside this repository the offset comes
# from another component of the same paths, and the bound's failure text says so.
# Outside this repository the question does not arise, because nothing is
# refused there — the consuming-project carrier reports and never blocks.
#
# ## The v11 roster cut, 2026-09-10 — five rows removed, one added
#
# This is the THIRD event in `helpers/growth-bound.ts` `## Re-baselining` — a
# merge of two lines that were each inside the bound — and it reaches exactly one
# row. `agents/coderev.md` and `agents/ontorev.md` merged into
# `agents/reviewer.md` at step C8 of the working-minimum cut. BOTH PARENTS WERE
# MEASURED INSIDE THEIR OWN BOUND AT THAT HEAD, which is the condition the event
# requires and not an assumption: coderev 182 514 against a row of 193 568, and
# ontorev 181 449 against a row of 192 521. The merged path measures 186 973.
#
# THE ROW WRITTEN IN IS NOT THE MEASURED TOTAL, AND THE DIFFERENCE IS ONE
# COMPONENT. Prompt and rules carry their measured values, 12 837 and 82 743.
# `CLAUDE.md` carries 93 432, the same figure every other row carries, rather
# than today's 91 393. It is a SHARED component: giving one row a smaller entry
# than its ten siblings would make that path the first to fail on any future
# CLAUDE.md growth, which is a bound on the project's instructions wearing a
# reviewer's name. So the row is 189 012, and the 2 039 between it and the
# measured total is head-room in `CLAUDE.md` that all eleven rows have.
#
# The step's own acceptance was tighter than this bound and is recorded because
# it is not reproducible from the numbers here: each merge had to be green
# against the SMALLEST pre-cut total among the paths it replaced. Reviewer's was
# 192 521 and the merged path is under it. The other three merges the step
# planned — planner absorbing shaper, analyst absorbing consultant, curator
# absorbing reconciler — were each measured against that same rule and STOPPED,
# so those five roles are still five agents and their rows below are untouched.
# The measurements that stopped them are in the C8 commit message.
#
# FIVE ROWS WERE REMOVED, and only two of them by merger. `agents/bugfixer.md`,
# `agents/playmaker.md` and `agents/taskplanner.md` were deleted with the
# subjects they served — the phase procedure, the Circle portfolio and the
# session work queue — and absorbed into nothing, so no row inherits their
# figures and nothing here was credited with their removal.
#
# THE SURVIVING ROWS WERE NOT RE-CUT AT THIS EVENT. Nine commits took real bytes
# off the rule set between the arming and this cut, so every surviving path then
# measured well under its row. Following the measurement down was none of the
# three events, and was deliberately not done here. The event below is what
# changed that, thirteen days later and for this bound alone.
#
# Provenance: capability C8 of the spec
# `260909-1615_*_spec-cut-fusion-to-a-working-minimum.md`, step A2 of
# `260909-1843_*_implementation-cut-fusion-to-a-working-minimum.md`.
#
# ## The re-arming, 2026-09-22 — every row follows the measurement down
#
# THE EVENT, AND IT IS THIS BOUND'S ALONE: after a cut of a component shared by
# every row, a zero-sum bound follows the measurement down. A zero-sum bound
# standing above the measurement refuses nothing and is not the instrument the
# HEAD-ROOM IS ZERO paragraph above describes. The 2026-09-16 `CLAUDE.md` cut
# took that shared component from 93 432 bytes to 8 021 on all eleven rows and
# left the tightest of them, curator, 43 536 bytes of slack.
#
# IT DOES NOT REACH THE THREE RATE SURFACES, and
# `helpers/growth-bound.ts` `## Re-baselining: the three events at which a
# baseline moves` stands unedited, heading and body. A rate bound's head-room is
# what its last cut left, which is event 1 there, and
# `260822-1154_*_does-a-cut-only-circle-re-baseline-the-surfaces-it-cuts.md`
# rules that for those surfaces and is not superseded by this. The condition
# that admits the event here is this bound's own definition, zero-sum, which no
# rate surface has.
#
# USED ONCE, HERE. Every row below is rewritten at the sizes measured at the
# commit that carries this paragraph, component by component, by the same
# summation the bound performs: `statSync` on the prompt, the sum of `statSync`
# over every path `bin/fusion-rules <name>` emits when run from this
# repository's root, and `statSync` on `CLAUDE.md`. Slack on all eleven rows is
# therefore zero, which is the point of the event: the next always-on addition
# in this repository needs a cut of its own rather than finding 43 kB waiting.
#
# THE ROWS DID NOT ALL MOVE ONE WAY, and the two directions are named rather
# than left inside one falling total. The shared `CLAUDE.md` component falls
# 93 432 -> 8 021 on every path. Three prompt components stand ABOVE their
# arming figures and are re-armed UPWARD with the rest: curator 34 554 ->
# 78 507, ontocoder 13 262 -> 15 875, coder 9 649 -> 12 165. Every row's total
# falls all the same, because the shared cut is larger than any prompt's rise.
# The per-row before and after figures, with their components, are logged in
# `README-hooks.md` `### Growth bounds on the shipped text`, which the ruling
# requires and which this file does not restate.
#
# Ruled by the user at 260922-1220, option 1 of
# `260922-0922_*_are-the-dispatch-path-rows-re-armed-at-the-post-cut-totals-and-under-which-event.md`.

